      <title>'Chilling effect:' West Michigan employers worried by changing visa guidelines</title>
      <link>https://www.woodtv.com/news/grand-rapids/chilling-effect-west-michigan-employers-worried-by-changing-visa-guidelines/</link>
      <description>A Sept. 19 presidential order increased the cost of the H-1B — a temporary, nonimmigrant visa designed to bring people with “specialty occupations” to the U.S. — petition fee from an average of $2,000 to $5,000 depending on the size of an employer to a flat fee of $100,000 for most new applicants applying from outside the country.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.woodtv.com/news/grand-rapids/chilling-effect-west-michigan-employers-worried-by-changing-visa-guidelines/</guid>
